      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
          "content": "Several different exercise protocols are used to assess exercise-induced bronchoconstriction (EIB), and to measure peak oxygen uptake (VO(2 peak)) and peak minute ventilation (VE(peak))."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "The aim of this study was to evaluate if one single test protocol for assessing EIB can also be used to determine aerobic capacity measured by VO(2 peak) and VE(peak)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "In a randomised cross-over design, 40 healthy subjects (female symbol/male symbol = 17/23) aged 14-40 years performed two exercise tests on a treadmill. Twenty subjects (female symbol/male symbol = 7/13) performed the two exercise tests at a treadmill inclination of 10.5%; the remaining 20 subjects (female symbol/male symbol = 10/10) performed at an inclination of 5.3%. A common stepwise protocol with 20 min of warming up was compared to an EIB test protocol of an 8-min treadmill run without warming up, with a workload corresponding to 95% of maximum heart rate during the last 4 min."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "VO(2 peak) did not differ significantly between the two test protocols at 10.5% inclination: 63.3 mL/kg min(-1)(59.3, 67.4) [mean (95% confidence intervals)] and 63.9 mL/kg min(-1) (60.0, 68.0), respectively, or at 5.3% inclination: 56.0 mL/kg min(-1) (52.1, 60.0) and 56.1 mL/kg min(-1) (51.9, 60.2), respectively. Also, VE(peak) did not differ between the protocols 158 (144, 173) vs 161 L/min (145, 176) at 10.5% inclination and 123 (114, 132) vs 127 L/min (116, 138) at 5.3% inclination, with the EIB protocol and the stepwise protocol, respectively."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "VO(2 peak) and VE(peak) did not differ between the two test protocols, and one single standardised EIB test may thus be used both for both provoking EIB and assessing VO(2 peak)."
        }
      ]},
